- 发布方/作者：University of Cincinnati / Griffin Warrior Project  
- 日期：未标明（项目介绍页面，内容与2015后期报道相符）  
- 来源类型：大学考古项目官网  
- 触发查询：Ring of Nestor gold ring Mycenaean discovery location tomb Nestor 
Pylos  
- 相关性说明：官方项目页面，系统讲述“Griffin 
Warrior”墓的位置、发现过程和年代，为戒指的考古背景、文化归属提供基础。  
- 摘录：  
  1. “In May 2015, archaeologists from the University of Cincinnati discovered 
an intact Bronze Age shaft grave at Pylos in southwestern Greece, near the 
so‑called Palace of Nestor.”  
  2. “The grave, dubbed the ‘Griffin Warrior’ tomb, dates to about 1500 B.C. and
predates the construction of the palace by some two centuries.”  
  3. “The burial contained an adult male, about 30–35 years old, accompanied by 
hundreds of grave offerings in gold, silver, bronze, and semiprecious stones.”  
  4. “Among the most spectacular finds are several gold rings and finely 
engraved sealstones that show scenes of combat and ritual.”  

