"20260628171343001461_ae7be229", "type": "Evidence", "text": "论文将“Ring of 
Nestor”归为一组米诺斯或迈锡尼金质印章戒指，用以展示贵族墓葬中的宗教仪式或神话场
景，并指出这些图像在理解“after‑life”观念方面的重要性。", "source_ids": 
["20260628171339938421_ee224af1"], "citations": [19]}, {"id": 
"20260628171343082655_1060b947", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"作者提到，学界过去对“Ring of 
Nestor”的真实性持怀疑态度，而新出土戒指与其在图像和工艺上的强对比为其真实性提供
了新的论据，强化了其在探讨爱琴世界精英葬俗、金器工艺和宗教象征中的标志性地位。",
 "source_ids": ["20260628171339938421_ee224af1"], "citations": [19]}, {"id": 
"20260628171358569532_54f0a1fa", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 'Ring of Nestor' 
is a gold signet ring, treated in scholarship as a key example of Minoan or 
Mycenaean-style gold signet rings from a sepulchral context at Thisbê in Boeotia
and associated more broadly with the Pylos region.", "source_ids": 
["20260628170909519788_a01c45aa", "20260628171339806409_fa8217b3", 
"20260628171339876710_e202618c", "20260628171339908709_309f4c44"], "citations": 
[4, 16, 17, 18]}, {"id": "20260628171358836762_2ec7b03c", "type": "Claim", 
"text": "The 'Ring of Nestor' bears a complex figural scene with trees, human 
figures and supernatural motifs, which scholars use as a key iconographic case 
for exploring Minoan and Mycenaean religious imagery, elite funerary symbolism, 
and ideas of the afterlife.", "source_ids": ["20260628170909519788_a01c45aa", 
"20260628171339806409_fa8217b3", "20260628171339876710_e202618c", 
"20260628171339908709_309f4c44", "20260628171339938421_ee224af1"], "citations": 
[4, 16, 17, 18, 19]}], "offset": 0, "limit": 50, "total": 18, "next_offset": 
null}
