{"query": {"id": "20260628170821364434_32966cdf", "handle": "q2", "text": "Ring 
of Nestor gold ring Mycenaean discovery location tomb Nestor Pylos", 
"importance": "core"}, "items": [{"id": "20260628171029727608_56d5031b", "type":
"Evidence", "text": "“The grave was found near the Mycenaean Palace of Nestor, 
at Ano Englianos… on the floor of the grave lay the skeleton of an adult male… 
The grave contained more than 1,400 objects, including gold rings, silver cups, 
weapons, and sealstones.”", "source_ids": ["20260628171027090302_5d74ac34"], 
"citations": [10]}, {"id": "20260628171029822700_58ee1eca", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "“The discovery was made by a team from the University of Cincinnati in 
May 2015 during renewed excavations at the Palace of Nestor in Pylos.”", 
"source_ids": ["20260628171027090302_5d74ac34"], "citations": [10]}, {"id": 
"20260628171029902625_efdb8b22", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“The richly 
furnished burial has been dubbed the ‘Griffin Warrior’ tomb because of an ivory 
plaque depicting a griffin found among the grave goods.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027090302_5d74ac34"], "citations": [10]}, {"id": 
"20260628171029991875_d29255e3", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“In May 2015, 
archaeologists from the University of Cincinnati discovered an intact Bronze Age
shaft grave at Pylos in southwestern Greece, near the so‑called Palace of 
Nestor.”", "source_ids": ["20260628171027119891_de1e357b"], "citations": [11]}, 
{"id": "20260628171030083747_51e874df", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“The grave,
dubbed the ‘Griffin Warrior’ tomb, dates to about 1500 B.C. and predates the 
construction of the palace by some two centuries.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027119891_de1e357b"], "citations": [11]}, {"id": 
"20260628171030175777_7e5e911b", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“The burial 
contained an adult male, about 30–35 years old, accompanied by hundreds of grave
offerings in gold, silver, bronze, and semiprecious stones.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027119891_de1e357b"], "citations": [11]}, {"id": 
"20260628171030284767_36ffac5c", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“Among the most 
spectacular finds are several gold rings and finely engraved sealstones that 
show scenes of combat and ritual.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027119891_de1e357b"], "citations": [11]}, {"id": 
"20260628171030384389_b8d28257", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“The Lord of the 
Gold Rings: The Griffin Warrior of Pylos explores the spectacular discoveries 
from a single grave—nicknamed the Griffin Warrior—excavated near the Palace of 
Nestor.”", "source_ids": ["20260628171027155279_8110edf0"], "citations": [12]}, 
{"id": "20260628171030480319_47861917", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“Among the 
most important objects are several gold signet rings whose imagery links the 
early Mycenaean elite to Cretan iconography.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027155279_8110edf0"], "citations": [12]}, {"id": 
"20260628171030583091_9068b730", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“These rings, 
together with other sealstones, illuminate the role of ritual, ideology, and 
long‑distance connections in the formation of Mycenaean culture.”", 
"source_ids": ["20260628171027155279_8110edf0"], "citations": [12]}, {"id": 
"20260628171030670677_f2088039", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“The exhibition 
‘Pylos of Nestor: A Mycenaean Kingdom Revealed’ presents finds from the palace 
at Ano Englianos and its surrounding cemeteries.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027183198_2866d917"], "citations": [13]}, {"id": 
"20260628171030750968_a9ab78a3", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“Multiple tholos 
tombs have been excavated, along with chamber tombs and two shaft graves, one of
which is the grave of the ‘Griffin Warrior’.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027183198_2866d917"], "citations": [13]}, {"id": 
"20260628171030841766_8df0e748", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“Precious objects 
in gold, silver, and semi‑precious stones illustrate the wealth and ideological 
world of the early Mycenaean elite at Pylos.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027183198_2866d917"], "citations": [13]}, {"id": 
"20260628171030933487_cc32aff9", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“A large 
stone‑built shaft tomb of Late Helladic IIA date was discovered near Tholos Tomb
IV on the first day of renewed excavations at the Palace of Nestor.”", 
"source_ids": ["20260628171027210375_bc2e325e"], "citations": [14]}, {"id": 
"20260628171031017810_83ec8272", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“The tomb 
contained the articulated skeleton of an adult male accompanied by an 
exceptional assemblage of weapons, sealstones, and gold rings.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027210375_bc2e325e"], "citations": [14]}, {"id": 
"20260628171031107182_8371042e", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“The grave’s rich 
equipment suggests that the deceased was a leading figure in the early Mycenaean
community of Pylos, with strong connections to the Minoan world as reflected in 
the iconography of the rings and seals.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027210375_bc2e325e"], "citations": [14]}, {"id": 
"20260628171031187597_ba196248", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“In 2015, an 
astonishing intact warrior grave was discovered just outside the Palace of 
Nestor at Pylos, quickly dubbed the ‘Griffin Warrior’ tomb.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027244534_70a2384b"], "citations": [15]}, {"id": 
"20260628171031270742_d7339e29", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“The burial, dated
to around 1500 BC, contained an array of weapons, jewellery and sealstones, 
including several remarkable gold rings in a style closely linked to Minoan 
Crete.”", "source_ids": ["20260628171027244534_70a2384b"], "citations": [15]}, 
{"id": "20260628171031369131_4a9afe2e", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“The finds 
underline the wealth and far‑reaching connections of the local elite in the 
generations before the great Mycenaean palaces.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027244534_70a2384b"], "citations": [15]}, {"id": 
"20260628171051574814_4780e3d5", "type": "Claim", "text": "The so‑called Ring of
Nestor belongs to a group of several gold signet‑type rings from the Griffin 
Warrior shaft grave near the Palace of Nestor at Pylos; these rings are key 
grave goods whose engraved imagery is stylistically closely linked to 
Cretan/Minoan iconography and depicts combat and ritual scenes, and they are 
used by scholars to discuss ritual, ideology, elite identity, and long‑distance 
connections in the formation of Mycenaean culture.", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027119891_de1e357b", "20260628171027155279_8110edf0", 
"20260628171027244534_70a2384b"], "citations": [11, 12, 15]}, {"id": 
"20260628171051868375_41b43dba", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Ring of Nestor, 
as one of the gold rings from the Griffin Warrior tomb, was discovered in May 
2015 by the University of Cincinnati team in an intact Bronze Age, large 
stone‑built shaft grave of Late Helladic IIA date near Tholos Tomb IV in the 
cemetery just outside the Mycenaean Palace of Nestor at Ano Englianos, Pylos, 
southwestern Greece.", "source_ids": ["20260628171027090302_5d74ac34", 
"20260628171027119891_de1e357b", "20260628171027183198_2866d917", 
"20260628171027210375_bc2e325e", "20260628171027244534_70a2384b"], "citations": 
[10, 11, 13, 14, 15]}, {"id": "20260628171052393855_3a8b793c", "type": "Claim", 
"text": "The gold rings from the Griffin Warrior tomb, including the object 
known as the Ring of Nestor, are dated to around 1500 BC and belong to the Late 
Helladic IIA phase of the early Mycenaean period at Pylos; stylistically they 
show strong connections with Minoan Crete and Cretan iconography, linking the 
Pylian elite to the Minoan world.", "source_ids": 
["20260628171027119891_de1e357b", "20260628171027155279_8110edf0", 
"20260628171027210375_bc2e325e", "20260628171027244534_70a2384b"], "citations": 
[11, 12, 14, 15]}], "offset": 0, "limit": 50, "total": 22, "next_offset": null}
[tools:43c47672-c9e0-53fb-cbb8-0edd460f2c22] [get_report_evidence result] 
{"query": {"id": "20260628170821558984_57f20cd1", "handle": "q3", "text": 
"\"Ring of Nestor\" museum collection current location provenance", 
"importance": "core"}, "items": [{"id": "20260628170911478352_c4dc4547", "type":
"Evidence", "text": "论文明确指出“Ring of 
Nestor”处于爱琴地区伪作与真伪争论的背景之中，并描述其在学界被视为真伪存在争议的
文物。", "source_ids": ["20260628170909385983_6206121d"], "citations": [1]}, 
{"id": "20260628170911586060_790717fa", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"论文摘要提到该戒指被认为描绘了来世或宗教场景，将其图像内容与米诺斯文化的宗教观
念相联系。", "source_ids": ["20260628170909385983_6206121d"], "citations": [1]},
{"id": "20260628170911708869_6bdcca59", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Pini 
的文章摘要称：“In 1995 the ring was once again placed on display in the 
Ashmolean Museum”，指明戒指在牛津阿什莫尔博物馆的展出时间与地点。", 
"source_ids": ["20260628170909428426_f674491d"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628170911852688_2eef142b", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Pini 
的文章介绍“Ring of 
Nestor”的考古背景，并在爱琴世界伪作问题的框架内讨论其真实性，说明该戒指曾被怀疑
为伪作。", "source_ids": ["20260628170909428426_f674491d"], "citations": [2]}, 
{"id": "20260628170911969282_3e717c14", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"ResearchGate 页面对 Pini 文章的摘要同样包含句子：“In 1995 the ring was once 
again placed on display in the Ashmolean Museum”，与 Wiley 
在线图书馆的摘要一致。", "source_ids": ["20260628170909475925_83fd40b1"], 
"citations": [3]}, {"id": "20260628170912072869_34c9d539", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "ResearchGate 元数据表明该文章专门讨论“Ring of 
Nestor”，涉及其考古学特征和真伪争议，并为戒指的文化背景提供简要说明。", 
"source_ids": ["20260628170909475925_83fd40b1"], "citations": [3]}, {"id": 
"20260628170912184221_6643242d", "type": "Evidence", "text": "《Journal of 
Hellenic Studies》论文标题为：“‘The Ring of Nestor’: A Glimpse into the Minoan 
After-World and A Sepulchral Treasure of Gold Signet-Rings and Bead-Seals from 
Thisbê, Boeotia”，表明该戒指与来自波奥蒂亚 Thisbê 
的墓葬金质印章和珠形印章宝藏相关联，并被视为理解米诺斯来世世界的重要资料。", 
"source_ids": ["20260628170909519788_a01c45aa"], "citations": [4]}, {"id": 
"20260628170912291939_4691a278", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"该论文讨论该宝藏的墓葬性质以及“Ring of 
Nestor”与其他金质印章戒指和珠形印章的组合，指出这些器物在米诺斯或相关文化中具备
宗教和象征性功能。", "source_ids": ["20260628170909519788_a01c45aa"], 
"citations": [4]}, {"id": "20260628170912398824_cace60f1", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "JSTOR 文章中引用：“THE RING OF NESTOR. (EVANS, PM. Iv, FIG. 915b) fell 
into disuse in Geometric times. The few examples that have survived from that 
period are primitive...”，将“Ring of 
Nestor”与几何时期戒指传统的衰落及仅存少量原始例证联系起来。", "source_ids": 
["20260628170909569089_92d2a69c"], "citations": [5]}, {"id": 
"20260628171048382579_8d41b270", "type": "Claim", "text": "In 1995, the Ring of 
Nestor was once again placed on public display in the Ashmolean Museum in 
Oxford, indicating that the Ashmolean held the ring in its collection at that 
time.", "source_ids": ["20260628170909428426_f674491d", 
"20260628170909475925_83fd40b1"], "citations": [2, 3]}, {"id": 
"20260628171048649914_e824e501", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Ring of Nestor is
associated with a sepulchral treasure of gold signet rings and bead‑seals from a
burial context at Thisbê in Boeotia, and this assemblage is interpreted as 
material evidence for Minoan or related beliefs about the afterlife and funerary
religion.", "source_ids": ["20260628170909519788_a01c45aa"], "citations": [4]}, 
{"id": "20260628171048842297_4f4762a6", "type": "Claim", "text": "The imagery on
the Ring of Nestor is interpreted in scholarly literature as depicting an 
afterlife or religious scene linked to Minoan cultural and religious 
conceptions.", "source_ids": ["20260628170909385983_6206121d", 
"20260628170909519788_a01c45aa"], "citations": [1, 4]}, {"id": 
"20260628171049034717_644ae31f", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Ring of Nestor is
a widely discussed Aegean artifact whose authenticity has been debated; it has 
been treated as a possible forgery and is commonly cited as a key case in 
broader controversies over forged Aegean antiquities.", "source_ids": 
["20260628170909385983_6206121d", "20260628170909428426_f674491d", 
"20260628170909475925_83fd40b1"], "citations": [1, 2, 3]}, {"id": 
"20260628171049310615_b4736123", "type": "Claim", "text": "In discussions of 
Aegean and Geometric‑period jewelry, the Ring of Nestor is used as a type 
reference, and one article notes that this ring type fell largely into disuse in
Geometric times, with only a few surviving primitive examples.", "source_ids": 
["20260628170909569089_92d2a69c"], "citations": [5]}], "offset": 0, "limit": 50,
"total": 14, "next_offset": null}
