'20260628170909519788_a01c45aa', '20260628171339806409_fa8217b3', 
'20260628171339908709_309f4c44', '20260628171339938421_ee224af1'], 'kind': 
'paragraph'}, {'text': 'Although detailed measurements are not always 
foregrounded in summaries, the ring is repeatedly classified among substantial 
gold signet rings whose size and craftsmanship mark them as high-status objects 
associated with aristocratic or princely burials.[4][16][18][19] Within this 
group, the Ring of Nestor is singled out for the density and narrative character
of its imagery, which has made it a standard example in iconographic studies of 
Aegean gold rings.[18][19]', 'source_ids': ['20260628170909519788_a01c45aa', 
'20260628171339806409_fa8217b3', '20260628171339908709_309f4c44', 
'20260628171339938421_ee224af1'], 'kind': 'paragraph'}]}, {'title': 'Discovery 
